ong subject) are in\n85\t   `tests/test_integrate_station.py`, which `TC-132` cites for `LLR-140` and\n86\t   `TC-205` does not cite at all. Either cite that module and say in the\n87\t   `Method` which arms it holds, or drive the two peels' divergence directly in\n88\t   `test_verdict_record.py`. Citing is the smaller change and is honest, since\n89\t   the arms genuinely exist. Citing a `SLOW_MODULES` member beside this row's\n90\t   `Tier = Smoke` is not a new contradiction: `test_integrate_admission` is\n91\t   already both, and `docs/registry-machinery-reference.md` §12.2 records\n92\t   `TC.Tier` and the pytest marker as deliberately unreconciled.\n93\t6. `TC-205.method`'s one factual misstatement of its own driving. It says \"a\n94\t   changed work blob and a changed `docs/work/` spec each fold DIFFERENT\", but\n95\t   `_listing` numbers blobs `{:040x}` (`tests/test_verdict_record.py:60-64`), so\n96\t   at `:81-90` the spec entry's sha ends `0002` and its path holds no `00001`:\n97\t   the `b\"00001\"` -> `b\"00009\"` substitution moves only `src/widget.py`, and the\n98\t   second assertion compares against `_listing(\"src/widget.py\")`, which DROPS\n99\t   the spec entry instead of changing it. Coverage is equivalent in effect\n100\t   because `fold_listing` folds the whole `<mode> <type> <sha>\\t<path>` line\n101\t   (`verdict.py:256`), so either fix the sentence to describe the dropped-entry\n102\t   assertion or change the fixture to match the sentence. Do not leave a\n103\t   `Method` claiming an assertion the test does not make.\n104\t7. `CMP-006`'s note, which THIS row falsifies and which therefore re-points with\n105\t   it rather than being deferred. The note reads \"kitlib/station.py (LLR-182) is\n106\t   the one package module NOT owned here: it stays CMP-008\". That was true while\n107\t   `LLR-182` was the only kitlib module at CMP-008; `LLR-207` places\n108\t   `kitlib/verdict.py` at CMP-008 too (both confirmed by reading the parsed\n109\t   reg